@startuml
title MEDORA: Invoice Lifecycle
!include ../../../../shared/templates/medora-style.puml
skinparam dpi 192
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam titleFontSize 22
state "Partially Paid" as PartiallyPaid
state RefundOutcome <<choice>>

[*] -down-> Draft : createFromEligibleItems()
Draft -down-> Issued : issue()\n[totals and price data valid]
Issued -down-> PartiallyPaid : recordPayment(amount, requestKey)\n[0 < amount < balance]\n/ append payment event
Issued -[hidden]right-> Paid
PartiallyPaid -down-> Paid : recordPayment(amount, requestKey)\n[amount = balance]\n/ append payment event
Issued -right-> Paid : recordPayment(amount, requestKey)\n[amount = balance]\n/ append payment event
PartiallyPaid --> PartiallyPaid : recordPayment(amount, requestKey)\n[0 < amount < balance]\n/ append payment event

Paid -left-> RefundOutcome : completeRefund(refundRef)
PartiallyPaid -right-> RefundOutcome : completeRefund(refundRef)
RefundOutcome -up-> PartiallyPaid : [0 < net paid after refund < total]\n/ append refund event
RefundOutcome -up-> Issued : [net paid after refund = 0]\n/ append refund event

note bottom of Paid
  Refunds are separate, auditable events that never edit the original
  payment. A refund still pending approval changes no invoice state.
  A completed refund returns the invoice to Partially Paid or Issued,
  according to the net paid amount.
end note
@enduml
